313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In this project, we aim to analyze and document the software engineering aspects of an existing application called Structured. Structured is a daily planner and visual calendar app that helps users organize their tasks and manage their time efficiently. The app allows users to plan their day using a timeline-based interface, where tasks are assigned to specific time slots.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The objective of our project is not to build a new system, but to study and understand how a real-world productivity app is structured from a software engineering perspective. This includes identifying stakeholders, documenting system requirements, analyzing its architecture, and modeling various components such as use cases and class diagrams.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The contribution of our work is to apply theoretical knowledge gained in the course to a practical case. By reverse-engineering Structured, we can explore how design patterns, requirement specifications, and UML diagrams apply to existing software. This enhances our understanding of system design and analysis through a real and useful application that is widely used in productivity and task management.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
